933:   Returns -1, 0 or 1. It encodes both values, so callers reserve it for the\n936:  (let [ea (encode a)\n937:        eb (encode b)\n1128:   apart (host identifier equality on ClojureScript compares the joined\n1158:              (refuse :malformed-frame \"identifier payload is not [ns name]\"))]\n1248:          39 (refuse :identifier-tag-39)\n1260:   `decode` accepted them, or bytes this codec encoded itself. Refuses\n1262:   but does not re-encode the value to prove canonicality -- that check\n1275:  \"The value of one canonical Jing payload (byte[], Uint8Array or\n1277:   refuses and also any payload whose value does not re-encode to exactly\n1281:    (when-not (bytes= bs (encode value))\n1282:      (refuse :non-canonical))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
